{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1344623-banishers-in-2e","id":1344623,"title":"Banishers in 2e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-30T03:06:01-07:00","id":1344623,"title":"Banishers in 2e","content":"So, how much have changed in Banishers with Second Edition out? They didn't really get more than one sidebar. Do they still infect other mages with Banisher &quot;condition&quot;? Do they still spontaneously develop Arcana and Rotes? Do they still get ancestral memories from supposed proto-Order of Timori? How much of 1e lore of Banishers really apply for the 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T04:56:59-07:00","id":1344632,"title":"","content":"Okay, so. Banishers have a chapter in the next book (Night Horrors: Nameless and Accursed) giving rules and some sample storyteller characters.<br /> <br /> There's multiple phenomena and classes of mages who destroy magic that the Pentacle and Seers sum up with the word &quot;Banisher&quot;, much as the only thing a Tremere and a ghost mage have in common is that they're both &quot;Liches&quot;.<br /> <br /> There's mages who have decided magic is evil on moral or philisophical grounds. There's mages like Logophages and Timori (who on 2e are just a Legacy, not a secret Order) who selfishly fuel their own powers by consuming magic. These account for most Banishers - nothing really special about them, mechanically.<br /> <br /> And then there's the Harrowed, who suffered a metamorphic Awakening in which the part of the Watchtower's process that replaces Integrity with Wisdom failed. Being a mage who still has an Integrity rating sucks on a &quot;living nightmare&quot; level; their own powers cause breaking points, and their Mage Sight, including the Peripheral sense for anything supernatural or understanding High Speech, is actively painful. They don't tend to live very long.<br /> <br /> Banishers don't get rotes without Order membership, same as any other Nameless (what that 1e mechanic represented is adequately covered by praxes). As for the common belief that being Harrowed is somehow contagious... You'll have to wait for the book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":18}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-02T07:08:31-07:00","id":1345432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1344623-banishers-in-2e?p=1344632#post1344632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's mages who have decided magic is evil on moral or philisophical grounds. There's mages like Logophages and Timori (who on 2e are just a Legacy, not a secret Order) who selfishly fuel their own powers by consuming magic. These account for most Banishers - nothing really special about them, mechanically.</div> </div> </div> </div>So those Banishers are completely represented by normal mage template with Mystery Cult Initiation merit? They don't have any Conditions forcing them to kill non-Banisher mages, and they can be (in theory) talked to and persuaded that killing other mages and destroying their isn't the best way to do in life?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-02T08:09:28-07:00","id":1345438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1344623-banishers-in-2e?p=1345432#post1345432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So those Banishers are completely represented by normal mage template with Mystery Cult Initiation merit? They don't have any Conditions forcing them to kill non-Banisher mages, and they can be (in theory) talked to and persuaded that killing other mages and destroying their isn't the best way to do in life?</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as any Mage can be convinced they and their Obsessions are wrong, I'd say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-02T08:33:15-07:00","id":1345439,"title":"","content":"Logophages and Timori in particular warp their souls into eating various metaphysical parts of Mages, so probably not if they\u2019ve set their sights on you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-02T10:41:00-07:00","id":1345452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1344623-banishers-in-2e?p=1345432#post1345432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So those Banishers are completely represented by normal mage template with Mystery Cult Initiation merit? They don't have any Conditions forcing them to kill non-Banisher mages, and they can be (in theory) talked to and persuaded that killing other mages and destroying their isn't the best way to do in life?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, given that they're Legacies, and Legacies involves warping your being/magical identity/Supernal Signifier* into alignment with that Legacy....<br /> <br /> No one's saying no, but no one's saying your odds are good.<br /> <br /> But they're Legacies, not just Mystery Cult Initiation merits. They might have Mystery Cult around them, probably do, and people who are in that and not the Legacies proper are probably gonna be more open to persusasion. Actual Legacy-Participating Members though deal with the above.<br /> <br /> *It's been a while since I read Awakening 2nd, and while I know it changes...not your soul, but something fundamental to you, I don't precisely remember what it is. I assume, like everything else, it does inevitably come back to changing that Supernal Symbol of Character's Self to some degree, but hey, could be wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-02T12:49:20-07:00","id":1345461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1344623-banishers-in-2e?p=1345452#post1345452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, given that they're Legacies, and Legacies involves warping your being/magical identity/Supernal Signifier* into alignment with that Legacy....<br /> <br /> No one's saying no, but no one's saying your odds are good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was referring more to &quot;regular mages inside small Nameless Order with doctrine based about killing mages&quot; than to those Left-Handed Legacies. Trying to persuade Timori to quit eating Gnosis is like going to the cage of feral tiger and try to persuade him to go vegan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-02T12:59:07-07:00","id":1345463,"title":"","content":"I believe the Legacy shapes the mage's Gnosis, which subsequently shapes their soul.<br /> <br /> It depends if you can focus them against actively harmful targets. If a Timori goes against other Left-Handed mages, Seers whose most egregious abuses are brought to light, then the Timori can be kept busy, but will probably need to be neutralized later.<br /> <br /> But a Logophage can be pointed against Abyssal Memes, like the Nemesis Continuum, mental incursions of the Lower Depths, etc. Maybe they can be the bulwark against early outsets of the Morphean Continuity, Unforgotten Scions, etc. So there is room to make them work alongside the Consilium, even if they are constantly suspected. But working under those conditions is the standard modus operandi of the Guardians.<br /> <br /> There is always the possibility of someone who came to resent their Legacy and actively try to abstain from practicing it (&quot;they didn't tell you everything when you joined&quot;), such as an Echo Walker who only learned later how they were supposed to commune with the Ones Before. But that really only works with some Left-Handed Legacies, it doesn't usually apply to cases like the Timori or other Banisher focused Legacies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 11-02-2019, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-02T13:04:48-07:00","id":1345464,"title":"","content":"I wonder how plausible it would be for the Harrowed to become a part of Banisher type legacies, as I assume that their magic eating abilities would hurt them as much as any other magic does...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-02T13:31:02-07:00","id":1345468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1344623-banishers-in-2e?p=1345464#post1345464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how plausible it would be for the Harrowed to become a part of Banisher type legacies, as I assume that their magic eating abilities would hurt them as much as any other magic does...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's plausible, at least they won't suffer Breaking Points from their attainments, though it would presumably still be painful because it would trigger their PMS to use them. As Dave mentioned though, Harrowed tend to burn out fast and messily, so it would be difficult to keep them going long enough to get far even if they could be initiated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-02T17:26:08-07:00","id":1345488,"title":"","content":"Dave, tell me about &quot;Night Horrors: Nameless and Accursed&quot; so that I can buy it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T03:30:41-08:00","id":1345569,"title":"","content":"Curing the Harrowed back into Sleepwalkers - the *one* use of Death of Magic Boon acceptable in polite mage society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"